TASK: Lint-analyse the SystemVerilog module below as Verilator --lint-only -Wall would.

MODULE: counter_up_down
SOURCE:
// ASSUMPTION: Clock is named clk and is rising edge active as per spec
// ASSUMPTION: rst_n is active low async reset, srst is sync reset (not used)
// ASSUMPTION: Enable is synchronous active high, up is synchronous direction
// GAP: Data path width DATA_W is 8 bits as per param DATA_W
// ASSUMPTION: Counter saturates at 0 and 255 without wrapping
// ASSUMPTION: Reset always sets count to 0 regardless of prior state
// ASSUMPTION: Output reflects current count value on clk edge via assign
// ASSUMPTION: No extra pipeline stages or complex control logic used
// ASSUMPTION: Always-ff blocks use <= for synchronous reset/async reset
// ASSUMPTION: always_comb used for combinational logic only
// ASSUMPTION: case statements include default branches
// ASSUMPTION: No latches present; all signals driven in every path
// ASSUMPTION: Parameters are declared with explicit sizes and defaults
// ASSUMPTION: Interface matches exactly the spec ports
// ASSUMPTION: Reset edge is correctly handled as async for rst_n
// ASSUMPTION: Enable and up are synchronous inputs
// ASSUMPTION: Counter increments on rising clock when en=1, decrements when en=0
// ASSUMPTION: Output is synchronized via assign to clk edge
module counter_up_down(
    input logic clk,
    input logic rst_n,
    input logic en,
    input logic up,
    output logic [7:0] count
)
// ASSUMPTION: Default reset value for count is 0
logic [7:0] reg_count;

// Internal control logic
// ASSUMPTION: reg_count holds current state, updated on clock edges
always_ff(
    @(posedge clk)
    .count(reg_count)
) begin
    // ASSUMPTION: Registers are reset to 0 when rst_n is low
    reg_count <= {1'b0};
    if (rst_n)
        reg_count <= {1'b0};
    else
        // ASSUMPTION: Update based on enable and direction
        case(en)
            1'b1: // Enable high -> increment if up, decrement if down
                if (up)
                    reg_count <= {4'hFFFE, 8'h00}[reg_count + 1];
                else
                    reg_count <= {4'h0000, 8'hFFFE}[reg_count - 1];

            0'b0: // Enable low -> decrement if up, increment if down
                if (up)
                    reg_count <= {4'h0000, 8'hFFFE}[reg_count - 1];
                else
                    reg_count <= {4'hFFFE, 8'h0000}[reg_count + 1];

            default: // No enable
                reg_count <= {1'b0};
        endcase

    // ASSUMPTION: Saturation at 0 and 255 handled by modulo-256 logic
    end

    // Assign output to reflect current count
    count = reg_count;
endmodule

VOCABULARY — `code` MUST be one of (extend only with named subtypes):
  UNUSED, UNDRIVEN, WIDTH, WIDTHCONCAT, WIDTHTRUNC,
  CASEINCOMPLETE, CASEOVERLAP, LATCH, IMPLICIT, MULTIDRIVEN,
  INITVAR, BLKSEQ, COMBDLY, REALCVT, TIMESCALE,
  PORTSHORT, PINMISSING, PINNOCONNECT, GENCLK, SYMRSVDWORD.

EVIDENCE RULES — every finding must be substantiated:
• `line` MUST be an integer ≥ 1 that points to a real line in the SOURCE above.
• `signal` MUST name an identifier that appears on that line (or "" if the
  finding is whole-module like TIMESCALE).
• `msg` is one sentence: what the issue is. Do NOT include a fix.
• If you cannot point to a concrete line and signal, do NOT emit the finding.

FALSE-POSITIVE GUARD:
• Do not flag `UNUSED` for ports — Verilator only flags unused INTERNAL signals.
• Do not flag `WIDTH` when the literal already carries an explicit size cast.
• Do not flag `LATCH` for `always_ff` blocks — they are flops by definition.
• Do not flag `CASEINCOMPLETE` for `unique case` with all enum values covered.

STATUS RULE — `status` is "PASS" iff `errors.length === 0`. Warnings alone never
trigger FAIL (that is the lint stage's policy, not the model's).

OUTPUT SCHEMA (produce exactly this shape):
{
  "tool":     "Verilator 5.x (AI analysis)",
  "status":   "PASS | FAIL",
  "warnings": [
    { "id": "W-001", "code": "UNUSED",   "sev": "warning", "line": 42, "signal": "tmp_q",  "msg": "<one-line description>" }
  ],
  "errors": [
    { "id": "E-001", "code": "IMPLICIT", "sev": "error",   "line": 17, "signal": "wr_en",  "msg": "<one-line description>" }
  ],
  "summary": "<e.g. 0 errors, 2 warnings — PASS>",
  "log":     "<one Verilator-style line per finding, joined with \n>"
}
